  "live_records": {
    "q-3600": {
      "dom_id": "step-q3600",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Factor $\\frac{1}{27}+{z}^{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}+{b}^{3}=(a+b)({a}^{2}-ab+{b}^{2}).\n$$\n\nNotice that we can write our expression as a sum of cubes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{27}+{z}^{3}={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{3}+{z}^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor our expression using the sum of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{27}+{z}^{3} & ={(\\frac{1}{3})}^{3}+{z}^{3} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}+z)({(\\frac{1}{3})}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot z+{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}+z)(\\frac{1}{9}-\\frac{z}{3}+{z}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
