    "q-37550": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37550",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Factor the expression $8{x}^{6}+27{y}^{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum of cubes formula is given by\n\n$$\n{a}^{3}+{b}^{3}=(a+b)({a}^{2}-ab+{b}^{2}).\n$$\n\nNotice that we can write our expression as a sum of cubes, as follows:\n\n$$\n8{x}^{6}+27{y}^{3}={(2{x}^{2})}^{3}+(3y)^{3}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor our expression using the sum of cubes formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}^{6}+27{y}^{3} & ={(2{x}^{2})}^{3}+(3y)^{3} \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2}+3y)({(2{x}^{2})}^{2}-2{x}^{2}\\cdot 3y+(3y)^{2}) \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2}+3y)(4{x}^{4}-6{x}^{2}y+9{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-37550-a",
              "type": "math",
